## Node identity and runtime flags for mcl_chess.
##
## The cookie is NEVER a literal here: it arrives from the box at run time (the
## compose file's required-variable guard refuses to start without it), so an
## image or a repository cannot carry one. The node name is kept because the Ra
## member identity is node(): a nameless node is pinned to nonode@nohost, and
## naming it later would change a live store's identity.
##
## ⚠ NOTHING BUT A PLAIN VARIABLE NAME MAY APPEAR IN DOLLAR-BRACE BRACES IN THIS
## FILE, COMMENTS INCLUDED. relx expands this file with an awk that derives its
## substitution pattern FROM the text between the braces, so a shell-style form
## such as a required-variable guard turns into a pattern that matches nothing,
## the loop cannot advance, and the container spins at one core for ever without
## printing a line. That is how this file's own first deployment failed
## (mcl-chess#9); mcl_chess_service_tests now pins the rule.
## ⚠ THE NAME DOES NOT DECIDE WHERE DISTRIBUTION LISTENS. `-name ...@127.0.0.1'
## is what epmd ADVERTISES; without this line the dist listener still binds
## every interface. The Containerfile sets ERL_EPMD_ADDRESS for the epmd half,
## and this line is the listener half.
-name ${MCL_NODE_NAME}@${MCL_NODE_HOST}
-setcookie ${MCL_COOKIE}
-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

+K true

## Async thread pool. Raise it only if this service does real file or port I/O;
## for CPU-bound work the schedulers are the resource that matters and this flag
## is not on that path.
+A 8
